From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 22:35:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_battmgr: OPLUS: keep PD 9 V at stock
 cool-down level 4, 9 V ladder

On the OnePlus Pad 4 a USB-PD charger reaches 9 V at the attach, but the
driver takes it back to 5 V every time iceland-thermal publishes a charge
cap (kmsg 7 and 8 Nov 2026: "back to 5 V (cool-down)" 12 s after every
boot and every few minutes after a "new setup for 9 V"). The cool-down
test was "host cap below 3300 mA", while the thermal service writes
3000 mA for stock's cool-down level 4 and above, which stock clamps to its
last PD entry: 9 V at 1500 mA input (oplus_chg_wired.c, cool_down >
cool_down_pdqc_level_max; cool_down_pdqc_vol_mv 5000 5000 5000 9000,
cool_down_pdqc_curr_ma 1200 1500 2000 1500).

- A host cap below 3000 mA is a cool-down to 5 V (levels 1-3, the
  connector's 1200 mA, the cold / warm regions as before); a cap from
  3000 mA up to below 3300 mA is level 4: 9 V stays at stock's level-4
  input current of 1500 mA. The owner's 20 W applies without a cap.
- After the 9 V contract the input current runs stock's ladder again at
  9 V (oplus_chg_set_input_current() does so after its voltage change)
  instead of being bounded by the 5 V ladder's result, which a cable
  that sags below 4.5 V at 5 V held to 1350-1750 mA. The AICL point at
  9 V stays ours (7.5 V). The top is min(the row, stock's level 4, the
  contract current): stock caps the input current at the fixed PDO's
  current (oplus_get_max_current_from_fixed_pdo(), iceland sets
  oplus,common-charge-icl-support); here the contract current is read
  from the UCSI supply (RDO operating current at a 9 V PDO), 2000 mA
  when unknown.
- From the attach poll, while 9 V stays: VBUS below 7.5 V under load
  takes the input current one step down; a source that leaves 9 V by
  itself gets the 5 V current at once and at most two new 9 V attempts
  per attach; level 4 lowers the 9 V current at once and its end runs a
  new setup.

The setup line keeps its fields and adds the 9 V ladder's VBUS, the
contract current and "cool-down level 4". Its "VBUS %u mV" field is the
last 5 V ladder reading, not VBUS after the 9 V request.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c | 243 +++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 207 insertions(+), 36 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
index 7a0603525198..7fd8a70eed45 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
@@ -481,6 +481,9 @@ struct qcom_battmgr {
 	bool pd_9v_again;		/* at 5 V for a reason that can end (cool-down) */
 	unsigned int pd_5v_tries;	/* 5 V requests sent since the last setup */
 	unsigned int pd_icl_5v_ua;	/* the input current to go back to 5 V with */
+	unsigned int pd_icl_9v_ua;	/* the input current in force at 9 V, 0 = no 9 V ladder ran */
+	bool pd_9v_capped;		/* lowered for stock's cool-down level 4 */
+	unsigned int pd_9v_lost;	/* the source left 9 V by itself during this attach */
 	/* the charge limit kept by the driver, see qcom_battmgr_oplus_limit_update() */
 	unsigned int chg_limit_end;	/* percent, 100 = no limit */
 	unsigned int chg_limit_start;	/* percent, 0 = CHARGE_CTRL_DELTA_SOC below the end */
@@ -2590,12 +2593,21 @@ static int qcom_battmgr_oplus_set(struct qcom_battmgr *battmgr, int property, u3
 /*
  * The cool-down reaches this driver as the host's charge current cap (constant_charge_current_max):
  * the guard writes the smallest of its temperature region's current, its USB-C connector cool-down
- * (1200 mA, level 1) and iceland-thermal's gear (1200 / 1500 / 2000 mA, levels 1-3). Any cap below
- * the PD row's charge current counts as a cool-down. That also takes the cold / warm temperature
- * regions (1959 / 1000 mA) to 5 V, which stock does not (OURS, the lower side: the cap does not say
- * which rule set it).
+ * (1200 mA, level 1) and iceland-thermal's gear: 1200 / 1500 / 2000 mA for stock's levels 1-3, and
+ * 3000 mA (its CHARGE_MA_HIGH) for level 4 and above. Stock clamps every level above its last PD
+ * entry to that entry (oplus_chg_wired.c: cool_down > cool_down_pdqc_level_max), and that entry is
+ * 9 V at 1500 mA input (cool_down_pdqc_vol_mv / _curr_ma level 4). So:
+ * - a cap below 3000 mA is a cool-down to 5 V (levels 1-3, the connector's 1200 mA). That also takes
+ *   the cold / warm temperature regions (1959 / 1000 mA) to 5 V, which stock does not (OURS, the
+ *   lower side: the cap does not say which rule set it);
+ * - a cap from 3000 mA up to below the row's 3300 mA is level 4: 9 V stays, at stock's level-4 input
+ *   current (1500 mA, 13.5 W; the owner's 20 W applies without a thermal cap only).
+ * Before this, every cap below 3300 mA meant 5 V, so any thermal gear with a charge level (gear 2 and
+ * up) took PD to 5 V and back every few minutes (kmsg 8 Nov, q91j/q91k: "back to 5 V (cool-down)").
  */
-#define ICELAND_PD_9V_FCC_MIN_UA	3300000
+#define ICELAND_PD_9V_FCC_MIN_UA	3000000
+#define ICELAND_PD_COOL4_FCC_MAX_UA	3300000	/* caps in [3000, 3300) mA: stock's cool-down level 4 */
+#define ICELAND_PD_COOL4_ICL_MA		1500	/* cool_down_pdqc_curr_ma level 4, at 9 V */
 #define ICELAND_PD_5V_TRIES		3	/* 5 V requests per attach the charger may ignore */
 /* type changes followed during one attach; one more puts the "unknown" limits in force until the unplug */
 #define ICELAND_TYPE_CHANGES_MAX	5
@@ -2659,6 +2671,56 @@ static bool qcom_battmgr_iceland_pd_cool_down(struct qcom_battmgr *battmgr)
 	return battmgr->chg_fcc_host_ua && battmgr->chg_fcc_host_ua < ICELAND_PD_9V_FCC_MIN_UA;
 }
 
+/* stock's cool-down level 4 applies: 9 V stays, at ICELAND_PD_COOL4_ICL_MA; lock held */
+static bool qcom_battmgr_iceland_pd_cool4(struct qcom_battmgr *battmgr)
+{
+	return battmgr->chg_fcc_host_ua >= ICELAND_PD_9V_FCC_MIN_UA &&
+	       battmgr->chg_fcc_host_ua < ICELAND_PD_COOL4_FCC_MAX_UA;
+}
+
+/*
+ * The current of the 9 V contract the firmware made, as UCSI reports it (the RDO's operating
+ * current, with the selected source PDO's voltage): stock caps the input current at the source's
+ * fixed PDO current for the voltage in use (oplus_hal_adsp.c oplus_chg_set_input_current(),
+ * oplus_get_max_current_from_fixed_pdo(); iceland sets oplus,common-charge-icl-support). Unknown (no
+ * UCSI supply, no PD operation mode, a voltage other than 9 V, a value below 500 mA): 2000 mA, 18 W
+ * at 9 V, the most every 9 V PDO of an 18 W or larger charger gives (fail low).
+ */
+#define ICELAND_UCSI_PSY_NAME		"ucsi-source-psy-pmic_glink.ucsi.01"
+#define ICELAND_PD_CONTRACT_UNKNOWN_MA	2000
+
+static unsigned int qcom_battmgr_iceland_pd_contract_ma(struct qcom_battmgr *battmgr)
+{
+	union power_supply_propval volt, curr;
+	unsigned int ma = ICELAND_PD_CONTRACT_UNKNOWN_MA;
+	struct power_supply *psy;
+
+	psy = power_supply_get_by_name(ICELAND_UCSI_PSY_NAME);
+	if (!psy)
+		return ma;
+	if (!power_supply_get_property(psy, POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_VOLTAGE_NOW, &volt) &&
+	    !power_supply_get_property(psy, POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CURRENT_NOW, &curr) &&
+	    volt.intval >= 8500000 && volt.intval <= 9500000 && curr.intval >= 500000)
+		ma = curr.intval / 1000;
+	power_supply_put(psy);
+
+	return ma;
+}
+
+/* the input current 9 V may take: the row (the owner's 20 W), the contract, stock's level 4; lock held */
+static unsigned int qcom_battmgr_iceland_pd_9v_target_ua(struct qcom_battmgr *battmgr,
+							 unsigned int type, unsigned int power_mw,
+							 unsigned int vbus_mv)
+{
+	unsigned int ua = qcom_battmgr_iceland_icl_ua(type, power_mw, max(vbus_mv, ICELAND_PD_MV - 500U));
+
+	ua = min(ua, qcom_battmgr_iceland_pd_contract_ma(battmgr) * 1000);
+	if (qcom_battmgr_iceland_pd_cool4(battmgr))
+		ua = min(ua, ICELAND_PD_COOL4_ICL_MA * 1000U);
+
+	return ua;
+}
+
 /*
  * constant_charge_current_max: the host can lower the charge current (never raise it above the attach value).
  * 0 is refused rather than read as "no cap": use charge_behaviour to stop charging.
@@ -2880,41 +2942,124 @@ static unsigned int qcom_battmgr_iceland_aicl(struct qcom_battmgr *battmgr, unsi
 }
 
 /*
- * At 9 V: from the ladder's top step (2000 mA, 18 W at 9 V) up to the PD row's 9 V current
- * (the owner's 20 W, see ICELAND_PD_POWER_MW). Only after the 5 V ladder held its top step,
- * and kept only while the source holds it: no VBUS collapse and VBUS at ICELAND_PD_9V_AICL_MV
- * or above 50 ms after the write. Anything else (refused write, collapse, low or unreadable
- * VBUS) goes back to @icl_ua. Returns the input current in force. Called with the lock held.
+ * The input current ladder at 9 V. Stock runs its ladder again after the PD voltage change
+ * (oplus_chg_set_input_current(): the same usb_icl[] steps from 500 mA, 50 ms each, VBUS collapse
+ * and AICL point checked), so the 5 V ladder's result does not bound the 9 V current: a cable or
+ * source that sags below the 4.5 V point at 1.35 A at 5 V (kmsg 7 Nov: AICL 1350-1750 mA, VBUS
+ * 4.42-4.50 V) is no limit at 9 V. OURS: the point is ICELAND_PD_9V_AICL_MV (7.5 V), not stock's
+ * 4.5 V, so a 9 V source that sags stops the ladder long before the PMIC's own AICL would act.
+ * Steps: stock's usb_icl[] up to @target_ua, then @target_ua itself (at most 2220 mA, the owner's
+ * 20 W). Returns the input current in force: the last held step, or the 500 mA floor if none held
+ * (the poll's 9 V watch then sees the low VBUS). Called with the lock held.
  */
-static unsigned int qcom_battmgr_iceland_pd_raise(struct qcom_battmgr *battmgr, unsigned int type,
-						  unsigned int power_mw, unsigned int vbus_mv,
-						  unsigned int icl_5v_ua, unsigned int icl_ua)
+static unsigned int qcom_battmgr_iceland_pd_ladder_9v(struct qcom_battmgr *battmgr,
+						      unsigned int target_ua, unsigned int *mv)
 {
-	unsigned int icl_9v_ua = qcom_battmgr_iceland_icl_ua(type, power_mw, vbus_mv);
+	unsigned int target_ma = target_ua / 1000, ma = 0, held = 0, i;
 	bool collapse_ok = true;
-	unsigned int mv = 0;
+	int ret = 0;
+
+	for (i = 0; ; i++) {
+		ma = i < ARRAY_SIZE(iceland_icl_steps_ma) ?
+		     min(iceland_icl_steps_ma[i], target_ma) : target_ma;
+		if (ma <= held)
+			break;
+		ret = qcom_battmgr_oplus_set(battmgr, OPLUS_USB_INPUT_CURR_LIMIT, ma * 1000);
+		if (ret || !qcom_battmgr_iceland_aicl_held(battmgr, ICELAND_PD_9V_AICL_MV,
+							   &collapse_ok, mv))
+			break;
+		held = ma;
+	}
+	if (ret)
+		dev_warn(battmgr->dev, "charger setup: 9 V input current limit %u mA failed: %d\n", ma, ret);
+
+	if (!held)
+		held = iceland_icl_steps_ma[0];
+	if (held != ma || ret) {
+		if (!ret)
+			dev_info(battmgr->dev, "charger: 9 V input current %u mA not held (VBUS %u mV), %u mA\n",
+				 ma, *mv, held);
+		ret = qcom_battmgr_oplus_set(battmgr, OPLUS_USB_INPUT_CURR_LIMIT, held * 1000);
+		qcom_battmgr_iceland_check(battmgr, ret, "9 V input current limit");
+	}
+
+	return held * 1000;
+}
+
+/*
+ * OURS: at 9 V, from the poll (every OPLUS_CID_IDLE_POLL_MS), once no rule takes PD back to 5 V.
+ * The 9 V ladder often runs with the charger off (the charge limit's hold, the guard's inhibit),
+ * i.e. without load, and the PMIC's AICL point (4.4-4.6 V) does not catch a 9 V source that sags:
+ * - VBUS no longer high (the source left 9 V by itself: a hard reset, an over-current cut): the 5 V
+ *   input current at once (the 9 V current at 5 V would be above the 5 V row), then 9 V again
+ *   through a new setup, at most ICELAND_PD_9V_LOST_MAX times per attach, then 5 V until the unplug;
+ * - VBUS below ICELAND_PD_9V_AICL_MV: one ladder step down (no step up again before the next setup);
+ * - stock's cool-down level 4 begins: its input current at once; it ends: a new setup, which runs
+ *   the 9 V ladder up again.
+ * An unreadable VBUS changes nothing here. Called with the lock held.
+ */
+#define ICELAND_PD_9V_LOST_MAX		2
+
+static void qcom_battmgr_iceland_pd_9v_watch(struct qcom_battmgr *battmgr)
+{
+	unsigned int mv, ua, i;
+	bool cool4;
 	int ret;
 
-	if (icl_5v_ua < ICELAND_PD_ICL_MA * 1000 || icl_9v_ua <= icl_ua)
-		return icl_ua;
+	if (qcom_battmgr_request_property(battmgr, BATTMGR_USB_PROPERTY_GET, USB_VOLT_NOW, 0))
+		return;
+	mv = battmgr->usb.voltage_now / 1000;
 
-	ret = qcom_battmgr_oplus_set(battmgr, OPLUS_USB_INPUT_CURR_LIMIT, icl_9v_ua);
-	if (!ret && qcom_battmgr_iceland_aicl_held(battmgr, ICELAND_PD_9V_AICL_MV, &collapse_ok,
-						   &mv))
-		return icl_9v_ua;
+	if (!qcom_battmgr_iceland_vbus_high(mv)) {
+		battmgr->pd_9v = false;
+		battmgr->pd_9v_lost++;
+		battmgr->pd_9v_again = battmgr->pd_9v_lost <= ICELAND_PD_9V_LOST_MAX;
+		ret = qcom_battmgr_oplus_set(battmgr, OPLUS_USB_INPUT_CURR_LIMIT, battmgr->pd_icl_5v_ua);
+		qcom_battmgr_iceland_check(battmgr, ret, "5 V input current limit");
+		dev_warn(battmgr->dev, "charger: the source left 9 V (VBUS %u mV, loss %u), input limit %u uA%s\n",
+			 mv, battmgr->pd_9v_lost, battmgr->pd_icl_5v_ua,
+			 battmgr->pd_9v_again ? ", 9 V again at the next setup" : ", 5 V until the unplug");
+		return;
+	}
+	if (!battmgr->pd_icl_9v_ua)
+		return;
 
-	dev_info(battmgr->dev,
-		 "charger: 9 V input current %u uA not held (%d, VBUS %u mV), back to %u uA\n",
-		 icl_9v_ua, ret, mv, icl_ua);
-	ret = qcom_battmgr_oplus_set(battmgr, OPLUS_USB_INPUT_CURR_LIMIT, icl_ua);
-	qcom_battmgr_iceland_check(battmgr, ret, "input current limit");
+	if (mv < ICELAND_PD_9V_AICL_MV) {
+		ua = iceland_icl_steps_ma[0] * 1000;
+		for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(iceland_icl_steps_ma); i++)
+			if (iceland_icl_steps_ma[i] * 1000 < battmgr->pd_icl_9v_ua)
+				ua = iceland_icl_steps_ma[i] * 1000;
+		if (ua < battmgr->pd_icl_9v_ua) {
+			ret = qcom_battmgr_oplus_set(battmgr, OPLUS_USB_INPUT_CURR_LIMIT, ua);
+			qcom_battmgr_iceland_check(battmgr, ret, "9 V input current limit");
+			dev_warn(battmgr->dev, "charger: 9 V sags under load (VBUS %u mV), input limit %u -> %u uA\n",
+				 mv, battmgr->pd_icl_9v_ua, ua);
+			battmgr->pd_icl_9v_ua = ua;
+			battmgr->pd_9v_capped = false;	/* a sag is not undone before the next setup */
+		}
+		return;
+	}
 
-	return icl_ua;
+	cool4 = qcom_battmgr_iceland_pd_cool4(battmgr);
+	if (cool4 && battmgr->pd_icl_9v_ua > ICELAND_PD_COOL4_ICL_MA * 1000) {
+		ret = qcom_battmgr_oplus_set(battmgr, OPLUS_USB_INPUT_CURR_LIMIT,
+					     ICELAND_PD_COOL4_ICL_MA * 1000);
+		qcom_battmgr_iceland_check(battmgr, ret, "9 V input current limit");
+		dev_info(battmgr->dev, "charger: cool-down level 4, 9 V input limit %u -> %u uA\n",
+			 battmgr->pd_icl_9v_ua, ICELAND_PD_COOL4_ICL_MA * 1000);
+		battmgr->pd_icl_9v_ua = ICELAND_PD_COOL4_ICL_MA * 1000;
+		battmgr->pd_9v_capped = true;
+	} else if (!cool4 && battmgr->pd_9v_capped) {
+		battmgr->pd_9v_capped = false;
+		/* the next poll runs the attach setup: the 9 V ladder up again */
+		battmgr->charger_configured = false;
+		dev_info(battmgr->dev, "charger: cool-down level 4 over, a new setup at 9 V\n");
+	}
 }
 
 static void qcom_battmgr_iceland_setup_charger(struct qcom_battmgr *battmgr)
 {
-	unsigned int type, power_mw, fcc_ma, icl_ua, mv;
+	unsigned int type, power_mw, fcc_ma, icl_ua, mv, mv9 = 0, contract_ma = 0;
 	unsigned int icl_ask_ua, icl_5v_ua, aicl_mv = 0, vbus_mv;
 	bool pd, want_9v;
 	int ret;
@@ -2938,6 +3083,8 @@ static void qcom_battmgr_iceland_setup_charger(struct qcom_battmgr *battmgr)
 	battmgr->pd_9v_again = false;
 	battmgr->pd_5v_tries = 0;
 	battmgr->pd_icl_5v_ua = OPLUS_USB_ICL_BOOT_UA;
+	battmgr->pd_icl_9v_ua = 0;
+	battmgr->pd_9v_capped = false;
 
 	/* the charger type as the sysfs path reads it on this firmware: USB_ADAP_TYPE, mapped */
 	ret = qcom_battmgr_request_property(battmgr, BATTMGR_USB_PROPERTY_GET, USB_ADAP_TYPE, 0);
@@ -2978,8 +3125,15 @@ static void qcom_battmgr_iceland_setup_charger(struct qcom_battmgr *battmgr)
 		return;
 	}
 	/* the input current in stock's steps at the VBUS in force: up to the type's limit, or the last step the source holds */
-	icl_ask_ua = qcom_battmgr_iceland_icl_ua(type, power_mw, vbus_mv);
-	icl_5v_ua = qcom_battmgr_iceland_aicl(battmgr, type, icl_ask_ua, &aicl_mv);
+	if (pd && battmgr->pd_9v) {
+		/* already at 9 V (a type change or an unsuspend during a 9 V contract): the 9 V ladder */
+		icl_ask_ua = qcom_battmgr_iceland_pd_9v_target_ua(battmgr, type, power_mw, vbus_mv);
+		icl_5v_ua = qcom_battmgr_iceland_pd_ladder_9v(battmgr, icl_ask_ua, &aicl_mv);
+		battmgr->pd_icl_9v_ua = icl_5v_ua;
+	} else {
+		icl_ask_ua = qcom_battmgr_iceland_icl_ua(type, power_mw, vbus_mv);
+		icl_5v_ua = qcom_battmgr_iceland_aicl(battmgr, type, icl_ask_ua, &aicl_mv);
+	}
 	icl_ua = icl_5v_ua;
 	mv = 0;		/* VBUS is only read after a 9 V request */
 	battmgr->pd_icl_5v_ua = min(icl_5v_ua,
@@ -2991,7 +3145,8 @@ static void qcom_battmgr_iceland_setup_charger(struct qcom_battmgr *battmgr)
 	 * ask above is the 9 V one and no request is needed (the poll's check goes back to 5 V
 	 * if needed). The ladder's top step at 9 V is 18 W.
 	 */
-	want_9v = pd && !battmgr->pd_9v && !qcom_battmgr_oplus_update_gauge(battmgr) &&
+	want_9v = pd && !battmgr->pd_9v && battmgr->pd_9v_lost <= ICELAND_PD_9V_LOST_MAX &&
+		  !qcom_battmgr_oplus_update_gauge(battmgr) &&
 		  battmgr->status.voltage_now < ICELAND_PD_9V_VBAT_MAX_UV;
 	if (want_9v && qcom_battmgr_iceland_pd_cool_down(battmgr)) {
 		/* 9 V once the cool-down ends, through the poll's check */
@@ -2999,7 +3154,9 @@ static void qcom_battmgr_iceland_setup_charger(struct qcom_battmgr *battmgr)
 		want_9v = false;
 	}
 	if (want_9v) {
-		icl_ua = min(qcom_battmgr_iceland_icl_ua(type, power_mw, ICELAND_PD_MV), icl_5v_ua);
+		/* before the contract: never more than the 5 V ladder held, the 9 V row, level 4 */
+		icl_ua = min(qcom_battmgr_iceland_pd_9v_target_ua(battmgr, type, power_mw, ICELAND_PD_MV),
+			     icl_5v_ua);
 		ret = qcom_battmgr_oplus_set(battmgr, OPLUS_USB_INPUT_CURR_LIMIT, icl_ua);
 		qcom_battmgr_iceland_check(battmgr, ret, "9 V input current limit");
 		/* no 9 V request unless the lower current is in place; then VBUS may be 9 V */
@@ -3032,15 +3189,24 @@ static void qcom_battmgr_iceland_setup_charger(struct qcom_battmgr *battmgr)
 									  icl_ua),
 						   "input current limit");
 		} else if (!ret) {
-			icl_ua = qcom_battmgr_iceland_pd_raise(battmgr, type, power_mw, mv,
-							       icl_5v_ua, icl_ua);
+			/* 9 V holds: the ladder again at 9 V, up to the row, the contract and level 4 */
+			contract_ma = qcom_battmgr_iceland_pd_contract_ma(battmgr);
+			icl_ua = qcom_battmgr_iceland_pd_ladder_9v(battmgr,
+					qcom_battmgr_iceland_pd_9v_target_ua(battmgr, type, power_mw, mv),
+					&mv9);
+			battmgr->pd_icl_9v_ua = icl_ua;
 		}
 	}
 	mutex_unlock(&battmgr->lock);
 
-	dev_info(battmgr->dev, "charger: type %u, input limit %u uA, charge limit %u uA, VBUS after 9 V request %u mV, AICL %u of %u uA, VBUS %u mV, VBUS at setup %u mV%s\n",
